INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7) [%{}, 0, :user, "6080860c-061d-4f12-860f-8ed961e76ae0", "# JavaScript app benchmark\n\nA Vite + React + TypeScript app is already generated and its dependencies\nare already installed, in the current working directory under `benchapp`.\nWork inside it. The app you build is the artifact being benchmarked: a\nmodern demo landing site for a fictional product of your choice. It is\nnot a tool for running benchmarks; no benchmark-themed features or copy.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Remove the stock Vite demo content — the logos, the counter button and\n   the \"click on the Vite and React logos\" copy in `src/App.tsx`, and the\n   template styling in `src/App.css` you do not want.\n2. The app's root component must stay the **default export of\n   `src/App.tsx`**. The hidden tests import it from there.\n\n## Requirements\n\nMobile and desktop views, and working light and dark themes, throughout.\n\n3. A top navigation bar with id `main-nav` that marks the current page's\n   link with `aria-current=\"page\"`, has a menu that works at phone widths\n   behind a toggle button with id `nav-toggle`, and a theme toggle with id\n   `theme-toggle` usable at both widths.\n4. A landing page with a hero.\n5. A countdown that starts at 100 and decreases by 1 every 5 seconds,\n   updating live, the number in an element with id `countdown`. The\n   five-second tick is a real interval in every environment, including\n   test — the hidden tests advance a fake clock and expect it to move; do\n   not gate the timer on an environment check.\n6. A newsletter signup form with id `signup-form` and one email input. An\n   invalid address shows an error in an element with id `signup-error` and\n   is not added. A valid address is added to a \"recent signups\" list with\n   id `signups` on the same page. The same address submitted twice shows\n   the error and is not added again. In-memory is fine; no backend.\n7. A stats strip with id `stats`: the number of signups in an element with\n   id `stat-signups` and the number of countdown ticks so far in an\n   element with id `stat-ticks`, both computed from live state.\n8. An activity feed with id `activity` whose entries are `<li>` elements,\n   newest first, at most 10, one entry per signup and one per tick.\n9. A reusable feature-grid component in its own file under `src/`, used by\n   the landing page.\n10. A second page at `/about`, linked from the nav, on the same layout.\n\n## Tests\n\n11. Created features must be tested: add your own tests under `test/` or\n    `src/`, run by `npx vitest run`.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The dev server must run on port 4099: `npm run dev -- --port 4099 --strictPort`.\n  Do not use any other port.\n- Do not stop or kill processes you did not start.\n- The dev server is long-running: start it with `background: true` and poll\n  the job.\n- When your own tests and `npx tsc -b --noEmit` and `npm run build` pass, reply\n  with a one-line summary. Do not re-verify: a green suite and a clean build\n  are the finish line.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:23:27.391707Z], "7df443b8-1393-42b3-961c-d5a3bce8783d"]
