INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 43, :assistant, "6080860c-061d-4f12-860f-8ed961e76ae0", "\n\nNow let me add a test setup file and write the tests.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "  test: {\n    environment: 'jsdom',\n    globals: true,\n    setupFiles: './vitest.setup.ts',\n  },", "old_string" => "  test: { environment: 'jsdom', globals: true },", "path" => "benchapp/vitest.config.ts"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-a41b30289f22c57a", "name" => "edit"}], "Now write tests. Use @testing-library/react, fake timers, jsdom. Also localStorage in jsdom exists, matchMedia exists.\n\nThe tests:\n- countdown moves after fake clock\n- nav aria-current\n- signup validation + dedup + list\n- stats computed\n- activity newest first max 10\n\nNeed setup for jest-dom? I'll avoid jest-dom matchers to keep simple, use plain expect. Actually let me add a setup file with jest-dom for better. But vitest config globals true, environment jsdom. Let me add setupFiles with jest-dom import and a matchMedia stub if needed. useTheme calls window.matchMedia which jsdom supports. localStorage supported.\n\nFake timers + React act: advancing timers triggers setState; need act(() => vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(...)). testing-library's fireEvent is wrapped. I'll use `act(() => { vi.advanceTimersByTime(5000) })`.\n\nLet me write the test file. I'll set setupFiles for jest-dom in vitest config.\n\nAlso need to reset window.location between tests since App reads pathname. Since I import default export from App and render, path defaults to jsdom's '/' which is 'http://localhost:3000/'. So path is '/'. Good for most tests. For about test I'll pushState to /about before render.\n\nLet me write tests. Need to import render, screen, fireEvent, within, act.\n\nFor the interval test: App has StrictMode? No, App is default export; test renders it directly without StrictMode. Good.\n\nL