INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) [%{}, 45, :assistant, "6080860c-061d-4f12-860f-8ed961e76ae0", [%{"arguments" => %{"content" => "import '@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest'\nimport { afterEach } from 'vitest'\nimport { cleanup } from '@testing-library/react'\n\nafterEach(() => {\n  cleanup()\n  window.localStorage.clear()\n  window.history.pushState({}, '', '/')\n})\n", "path" => "benchapp/vitest.setup.ts"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-b8cfc42ce38cca74", "name" => "write"}], "Round 18 of 128 — plenty of budget. Let me continue writing the setup and tests.\n\nvitest.setup.ts imports jest-dom. Note tsconfig.app includes only src; vitest.config.ts and setup are at root, picked up by tsconfig.node? Let me check tsconfig.node.json includes. Actually tsc -b builds app + node configs. vitest.setup.ts at root would need to be included somewhere or it's just not type-checked (fine, since it's only referenced by vitest). But if it's not in any tsconfig include, `tsc -b --noEmit` won't check it — good, no type errors from jest-dom types. But my test files under src/ would be type-checked by tsconfig.app and would need @testing-library types + jest-dom matchers types. To avoid type errors, I'll put tests in `test/` directory (not under src), so tsconfig.app's include:[\"src\"] won't type-check them. Then `npx tsc -b --noEmit` won't check them, avoiding type issues, while vitest still runs them.\n\nWait — requirement 11: tests under test/ or src/, run by npx vitest run. Putting in test/ is allowed. And tsconfig.app only includes src, so tsc won't complain about test files' use of jest-dom globals. Good, safer.\n\nBut vitest default include patterns: ['**/*.{test,spec}.?(c|m)[jt]s?(x)'] — test/ files match. Good.\n\nvitest.setup.ts uses `import '@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest'`. For that, setup file also is outside src so not type-checked. Good.\n\nLet me create setup file and test file.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:28:14.368529Z], "24ec70c8-d24f-4503-b043-49a362a0b003"]
